1. start with an empty array called result to hold our findings
2. loop through each element in array a
3. check if the current element from a is in array b. use the includes method
4. if it is, add it to result
5. once done looping, result has all the common elements
6. send back the result array

```javascript
function findCommonElements(A, B) {
  var result = [];
  for (var i = 0; i < A.length; i++) {
    if (B.includes(A[i])) {
      result.push(A[i]);
    }
  }
  return result;
}
```

that's it! that'll give you an array of all the integers found in both a and b. *tail wagging*
